<title>MEXICO: MEXICAN STATE EXPORTS TO JAPAN GROW IN 7 MOS.</title>
<headline>MEXICAN STATE EXPORTS TO JAPAN GROW IN 7 MOS.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's northern Sonora state exported more than 12,000 tonnes of pork to Japan in the first seven months of the year, compared to about 10,000 tonnes in the year-ago period, state agency Notimex reported.</p>
<p>The exports from five Sonoran companies drew income of $49.23 million, the agency said, quoting a report from the state agriculture ministry.</p>
<p>The state has a history of exporting specialized pork cuts to Japan. On May 6 Sonora was ruled free of hog cholera by the United States, to become the first Mexican state allowed to export north of the Rio Grande.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
